5&nbsp; https://www.aluminum.org/Recycling &nbsp;

Expanded SAYTEX ALERO ® Portfolio: Innovation that Starts with the Customer &nbsp;
Share 
LinkedIn 
WhatsApp 
X 
Email 
Copy Link 
Sept. 30, 2026 
&nbsp;
Driven by technological innovation, increasing performance demands, sustainability objectives, and evolving market expectations, the flame retardant industry continues to transform. This portfolio expansion is the result of extensive customer engagement and collaboration across the value chain. Albemarle's commercial, technical, and product teams worked closely with customers to understand the unique challenges they face across applications, and those insights directly informed the development of application-specific grades tailored to distinct performance and processing requirements.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The expanded portfolio introduces SAYTEX ALERO ® Fine™ , developed for textiles and adhesives applications, and SAYTEX ALERO ® Optima™ , developed for thermoplastics applications. These additions build on the success of the SAYTEX ALERO polymeric flame retardant platform and reflect Albemarle's commitment to delivering customer-driven innovation and long-term value.
"Our leadership in flame retardant innovation resulted in SAYTEX ALERO®. Designed to address customers’ evolving needs, it reflects Albemarle’s commitment to delivering next generation, high-performance solutions.”
The expanded portfolio includes:
&nbsp;
SAYTEX ALERO Fine 
Developed for textiles and adhesives applications, SAYTEX ALERO Fine is designed for customers seeking effective dispersion, formulation flexibility and high-quality surface finishes in flame-retardant coatings.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
SAYTEX ALERO Optima 
Engineered for thermoplastics applications, SAYTEX ALERO Optima is designed to provide formulation flexibility, processing benefits and optimized performance across a range of thermoplastic systems, while enabling reduced reliance on antimony trioxide (ATO).
" Our advanced polymeric flame retardant platform provides our customers with the benefits of superior technical performance and improved value-in-use with proactive regulatory considerations"
Albemarle will showcase the expanded SAYTEX ALERO portfolio at the FAKUMA International Trade Fair &nbsp;in Germany this October.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We look forward to connecting with customers and industry professionals to discuss how these application-specific solutions are helping address their evolving needs. If you plan to attend FAKUMA, we invite you to visit us and learn more.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
If you are not attending the event, visit our Polymeric Hub or contact us to learn more.&nbsp;
Albemarle
Polymeric BFR Innovation 
Polymeric BFRs are flame retardants engineered with a high molecular weight, enabling them to remain within a polymer matrix and reducing potential for migration.
Flame Retardants
Connectivity
Mobility
Offerings
Safety
Flame Retardants 
50+ years of advanced flame-retardant polymer solutions that help keep cars, devices, home and aircraft fire safe.
Products
SAYTEX ALERO® 
Designed to deliver the proven performance of bromine with significantly improved processing, durability and responsibility metrics, including enhanced formulation flexibility and reduced ATO dependency.

Update to the Integrated Reporting Hub
September 4, 2026
Mitsubishi Chemical Group has provided a wide range of financial and non-financial information through the publication of our integrated report, KAITEKI Report. To deliver information in a timelier and more accessible manner, we transitioned last year to a web-based approach to information disclosure.
&nbsp;
Through the Integrated&nbsp;Reporting Hub, a portal page that consolidates our financial and non-financial information, we provide a diverse range of content related to our value creation, including messages from management, feature articles, and various disclosure materials.
&nbsp;
We have recently updated our management messages and published a series of interviews with the heads of our business groups as a featured content initiative. As the Group shifts from a defensive stance to a more offensive, growth-oriented approach, the heads of each business group share their perspectives on the changing business environment and discuss how they aim to create value going forward.
&nbsp;
We will continue to provide timely and transparent information through the Integrated&nbsp;Reporting Hub. We invite you to explore the Hub and learn more about how Mitsubishi Chemical Group is creating value for society, customers, and shareholders.
Integrated Reporting Hub 
https://www.mcgc.com/english/ir/hub/index.html 
